      "parent_visual": {
        "decision": "Pass as bounded stylized candidate, retaining pronounced faceted-agave and repetitive-tile limitations. Geometry/theme broadly align; do not claim premium marketing finish equivalence or final user approval.",
        "hardware": "Brass corner caps and tall centered clasp retain marketing scale/layout. Open captures expose two rear hinges and separated released latch. No obvious detached hardware; fine fastening detail simplified.",
        "limitations": "README and brief describe invented regional combination and original repeat, not workshop-pattern fidelity or botanical precision. Interior and fasteners become less legible on mobile. Static comparison does not independently reverify technical acceptance.",
        "quality": "Strong cobalt/ivory/terracotta identity and complete chest silhouette; all four captures keep box, open lid and controls in frame.",
        "terrain": "Blue-green radial agave and terracotta soil island preserve marketing placement and theme. Runtime leaves are visibly angular, rigid and flat-faced compared with marketing curved, overlapping, textured leaves. Agave is small but recognizable on mobile; concealed behind the open lid is not evidence of omission.",
        "texture": "Regular cobalt flower tile grid and orange lid match broad marketing design. Runtime lacks much of marketing handmade surface variation, glaze/material richness and leaf speckle; tiles are highly repeated and lid framing can look wood-like. These are explicit stylization gaps, not authenticated Talavera craft."
      },
